     "<div dir=\"ltr\">hi,<div><br></div><div>i set up an multigroup model following <a href=\"http://people.ku.edu/~s044p855/catInvariance.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://people.ku.edu/~s044p855/catInvariance.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792431369877000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3pPAZxqW4BCxC65tpuZzy-\">http://people.ku.edu/~s044p855/catInvariance.html</a> </div><div><br></div><div>however, the model for configural invariance does not converge and i get very high coefficients for loadings, variances and thresholds of some indicators. what can be causes of such problems? i suspect that my sample is too small (n = 500, 2 groups, one factor with 9 indicators a 4 response categories) and that some categories might be too sparse. also, one group has a higher overall mean in factor scores than the other. </div><div><br></div><div>what would be appropriate strategies to find out, what the problems are? <span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">and are there strategies to deal with such problems? like collapsing categories?</span></div><div><br></div><div>thanks a lot!</div><div><br></div><div>this is my model:</div><div><br></div><div><div><span style=\"font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace\">Overall =~ item_1 + item_2 + item_3 + item_4 + item_5 + item_6 + item_7 + item_8 + item_9</span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace\">Overall ~ c(0, NA)*1</span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace\">item_1| c(item_1.t1.constr, item_1.t1.constr)*t1 + c(item_1.t2.constr, item_1.t2.constr)*t2 + t3</span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace\">item_2| c(item_2.t1.constr, item_2.t1.constr)*t1 + t2 + t3</span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace\">item_3| c(item_3.t1.constr, item_3.t1.constr)*t1 + t2 + t3</span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace